      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `data-\u003eaddr_prot_start` and `data-\u003eaddr_prot_length` are initialized to 0 and are never updated during boot (e.g. in `cros_flash_rtkfp_init`). If the device boots with protection already enabled, this shadow state will incorrectly allow writes/erases until `flash_set_status_for_prot` happens to be called.\n\nSince SPI write and erase operations are already slow, maintaining a shadow copy of the protection range is unnecessary and error-prone. Please delete `flash_check_prot_range`, remove `addr_prot_start` and `addr_prot_length` from `struct cros_flash_rtkfp_data`, and call `flash_check_prot_reg` directly in `cros_flash_rtkfp_write` and `cros_flash_rtkfp_erase` to always evaluate protection against the true hardware state.\n[🔗](http://go/tj/20e38d34-27ca-44a0-a808-baee6ac45590)",
