      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] This control flow can be further flattened to avoid duplicating the `data-\u003eall_protected` assignment logic inside the condition. Since `ret` is checked immediately after, we can make the success path completely linear:\n\n```c\n\t/* Set flash protection and enable SW protect. */\n\tif (all) {\n\t\tret \u003d cros_flash_rtkfp_protect_at_boot(\n\t\t\tdev, EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ALL_AT_BOOT);\n\t} else {\n\t\tret \u003d cros_flash_rtkfp_protect_at_boot(\n\t\t\tdev, EC_FLASH_PROTECT_RO_AT_BOOT);\n\t}\n\n\tif (ret) {\n\t\treturn ret;\n\t}\n\n\tif (all) {\n\t\tdata-\u003eall_protected \u003d 1;\n\t}\n\n\tret \u003d cros_flash_rtkfp_sw_protect(dev, true);\n\tif (ret) {\n\t\treturn ret;\n\t}\n\n\tdata-\u003esw_protected \u003d 1;\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/20e38d34-27ca-44a0-a808-baee6ac45590)",
